# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Builds a synthetic evaluation corpus of 120 capstone/thesis project descriptions
(title, abstract, objectives) modeled on common Philippine IT/CS capstone topics.

15 "base" topics are each written in two independently-paraphrased forms
(different sentence structure, synonym choices, framing) to serve as KNOWN
similar/duplicate-concept pairs (ground truth = SIMILAR). The remaining 90
topics are distinct, single-instance entries used to form KNOWN dissimilar
pairs (ground truth = NOT SIMILAR) when compared against anything else.

This is a constructed benchmark corpus for evaluating the similarity-service
pipeline -- NOT the institution's own archive (which does not yet have 120
real historical projects) -- and is documented as such in the manuscript.
"""
